#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "02ae40ba-a02c-5025-9597-1968322f2421" :question/math-academy-id "e-2279" :question/problem "In a ballet school, the ratio of the number of students with black hair to the total number of students is $5: 8$. If there are $25$ students with black hair, how many students are there in ballet school who don't have black hair?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}8}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}}{{\\color{red}8}}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students with black hair and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe know that there are $25$ students with black hair, so we want to make a numerator of $25$. We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}\\times 5}{{\\color{red}8}\\times 5} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}25}}{{\\color{red}40}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since there are $25$ students with black hair, there must be $40$ students at the ballet school. Of this amount, the number of students who do not have black hair is\n\n$$\n40 - 25 = 15\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "4aeb615e-16a1-5170-be5e-fe0f63a5d895" :question/math-academy-id "e-2280" :question/problem "In a Chicago hospital, the ratio of the number of boys born to the total number of babies born is $\\dfrac{4}{9}$. If $100$ boys were born in that hospital in a particular month, how many girls were born that month?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of the number of boys born to the total number of babies born is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{9}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of boys born and the denominator represents the total number of babies born.\n\nWe know that $100$ boys were born, so we want to make a numerator of $100$. We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $25$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}4}\\times 25}{{\\color{red}9}\\times 25} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}100}}{{\\color{red}225}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $100$ boys were born, $225$ babies were born during that month. Of this amount, the number of girls was\n\n$$\n225 - 100 = 125\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ccf9fe1-2ca0-571a-9a19-c77299cbba51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178878} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fb44c8-a0ff-5966-90d1-ea1618435057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178879} {:answer/id #uuid "1242c19a-8fad-5620-840c-9f5d85b71c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178880} {:answer/id #uuid "350fcdd3-08e5-573a-8461-e9b2566545fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178881} {:answer/id #uuid "49665566-fa96-5af9-bd23-8304722f65e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49665566-fa96-5af9-bd23-8304722f65e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178882} :answer-field/id #uuid "28469468-6fc2-52c5-a538-523e17d18e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178877}] :question/id #uuid "b6604770-26c5-5386-84c1-792391047167" :question/math-academy-id "q-59887" :question/problem "The ratio of girls to boys in a chess club is $2: 1$. If there are $10$ girls, then how many members does the club have in total?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c59ba6f6-4740-5694-b646-ac3053792599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178884} {:answer/id #uuid "463173dc-1b01-5650-90c7-3526db97079b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178885} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2ac047-4457-569a-8e43-99c4c816eb41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178886} {:answer/id #uuid "79ca2378-b680-5c59-a7fb-a43eb8b90846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178887} {:answer/id #uuid "79ffc13e-ffed-5ac2-be33-5b07eba9c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ffc13e-ffed-5ac2-be33-5b07eba9c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178888} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a46319f-5e83-5ed8-82b0-8a27a0343225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178883}] :question/id #uuid "9aff327a-3ab5-5bdb-b2ab-437fac7b7394" :question/math-academy-id "q-59895" :question/problem "There are $15$ students in a class, and $\\frac{2}{5}$ of them wear glasses. How many students do not wear glasses?"}]}
